                        "entry_id": "0ef78bbc-6b71-3e30-ba3b-cd3a66108f32",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A game derived from hurling, and resembling hockey, played in Scotland."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6029c66f-660d-400c-81f7-5a0c4fc3923e",
                                "sense_id": "029ce359-c348-3d0b-a0da-f338e32057d3",
                                "text": "Shinty, once a battle royal between villages, is still a far tougher game than hockey, its nearest Sassenach equivalent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "951ef73b-97d2-44a6-8208-7510679f7f8d",
                                "sense_id": "029ce359-c348-3d0b-a0da-f338e32057d3",
                                "text": "To the city's large population of Highlanders, it was a portal to home, a place where you could speak Gaelic and sing it, buy tickets to the Glasgow Skye Association's annual dance, squabble about shinty arrange a lift to Ullapool, read the classifieds in the West Highland Free Press."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "427a3a37-866e-35af-b754-f07302abcc3e",
                        "entry_id": "0ef78bbc-6b71-3e30-ba3b-cd3a66108f32",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The stick used to strike the ball in this game, similar to a hockey stick."
